    <string name="battery_explain">Based on the last 7 days. \"Background\" is the time an app kept working while you were not using it, the main cause of battery drain. Messaging, music and navigation apps normally have some. High values for other apps are not normal: tap the app, then Battery, and choose \"Optimized\" or \"Restricted\". On Samsung you can also add it to Settings › Battery › Background usage limits › Deep sleeping apps.</string>
    <string name="open_battery_settings">Open battery optimization settings</string>
    <string name="unused_explain">Apps you have not opened in the last %1$d days, biggest first. Uninstalling them frees space and stops their background activity.</string>
    <string name="cache_explain">Apps keep %1$s of cache in total. Android does not allow other apps to clear it directly: tap an app, then Storage › Clear cache. Clearing cache is safe; your data and login stay.</string>
